      },
      "lineNbr": 714,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-31T14:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This condition differs from the `is_twobyte_form \u0026\u0026 store` in `movaps()`. I would expect `movups()` and `movaps()` implementations to be closer.\n\nThis seems to be because operands with `!src.NeedsRex() \u0026\u0026 !dst.NeedsRex()` can be expressed with both 0xf 0x11 and 0xf 0x10 for `movups()` (both 0xf 0x29 and 0xf 0x28 for `movaps()`) and it does not matter which we choose. Even in that case, I\u0027d prefer to make the same choice in `movaps()` and `movups()` and make these functions more similar, maybe using a shared helper function.\n\n(Disabling the disassembly fallback in assembler tests, I can see that the new \"movups\" implementation actually generates the same code as the `clang` assembler but the old `movaps` implementation does not. I\u0027d prefer to update `movaps()` to avoid the disassembler fallback which slows down the tests.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 714,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 714,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "b172417b760204437d8b5a543e54ee3b752fb6a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
